  "result": "{\"seen_before\": false, \"matches\": [], \"answer\": \"I found no past ticket that reports this exact problem. Power Display switching to a different profile after the laptop wakes from sleep isn't reported in the archive. Two related tickets are about different problems. PowerToys#48774 is about a Light Switch-linked profile not being applied on wake, and PowerToys#47951 is about Power Display not working after wake. Please file this as a new bug. Include the PowerToys bug report ZIP, your dock and monitor setup, and whether the 'switch profiles when theme changes' option or a Light Switch schedule is enabled. That option could be what changes the profile on wake, so try turning it off to see if the profile then stays put.\"}",
